---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '2026-04-28';
---
<BaseLayout title="Terms — Atlasmc" description="Atlasmc terms of use.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-20">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-neutral-500">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-3 mb-6">Terms of use</h1>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">The desktop application</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
      The Atlasmc desktop application is licensed under
      <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[var(--color-accent-bright)] underline">Apache License 2.0</a>.
      You can use it, modify it, and redistribute it under the terms of that license.
      The full license text and the
      <a href="https://github.com/kodekaze1/atlasmc/blob/main/NOTICE" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[var(--color-accent-bright)] underline">NOTICE</a>
      file are bundled with the source code.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">This website</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
      Site copy and code are Apache 2.0 licensed unless explicitly noted. You may
      reference Atlasmc in articles, reviews, and educational content. You may not
      use the Atlasmc name or branding to suggest endorsement or affiliation we
      haven&rsquo;t granted.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">No warranty</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
      Atlasmc is provided &ldquo;as is,&rdquo; without warranty of any kind. The
      desktop app is open-source software written by volunteers; bugs may exist
      and the app may produce broken Minecraft worlds for some inputs. You use it
      at your own risk. We are not liable for damages arising from use or inability
      to use Atlasmc.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Token-related notice</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
      Cryptocurrency tokens carry significant risk and may be classified as
      securities in your jurisdiction. Nothing on this site is financial, legal, or
      tax advice. If we deploy a token, the smart-contract terms (immutable on
      chain) supersede any informal language on this site. Any sale, distribution,
      or trading of the Atlasmc token will be governed by the documentation we
      publish at that point and the applicable laws of your country.
    </p>
    <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed mt-3">
      You are responsible for understanding the regulatory status of cryptocurrency
      in your jurisdiction before participating in any token-related activity.
      Consult a licensed professional if uncertain.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Trademarks</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
      Atlasmc, the Atlasmc wordmark, and any future logo are trademarks of the
      maintainer. Apache 2.0 grants a copyright license but does not grant trademark
      rights. References to upstream Arnis are made for attribution purposes only.
      &ldquo;Minecraft&rdquo; is a trademark of Mojang Synergies AB; we are not
      affiliated with or endorsed by Mojang or Microsoft.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
      Questions about these terms:
      <a href="mailto:kodekaze1@gmail.com" class="text-[var(--color-accent-bright)] underline">kodekaze1@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500 mt-12">
      A more formal Terms of Service may replace this page closer to a token launch.
      For now this is the operative agreement between Atlasmc and its users.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
